1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,147
Bake a cake with two eggs or with four.

2
00:00:03,147 --> 00:00:04,407
The cake changes.

3
00:00:04,407 --> 00:00:08,305
Mix two gases in any amounts,
and one number never changes.

4
00:00:08,705 --> 00:00:11,882
More hydrogen, less iodine,
or only the product.

5
00:00:11,882 --> 00:00:15,354
At one temperature, the same
number appears every time.

6
00:00:15,804 --> 00:00:18,390
Diya doubles a tea recipe in her kitchen.

7
00:00:18,390 --> 00:00:20,828
Twice the milk, twice the tea leaves.

8
00:00:20,828 --> 00:00:22,502
The taste stays the same.

9
00:00:22,852 --> 00:00:26,101
Last time, the amounts stopped
changing at equilibrium.

10
00:00:26,101 --> 00:00:27,834
But do they follow a rule?

11
00:00:28,334 --> 00:00:32,901
By the end, you will know that rule,
and the number that never changes:

12
00:00:32,901 --> 00:00:34,520
the equilibrium constant.

13
00:00:35,170 --> 00:00:36,560
Think of a recipe.

14
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:38,411
The amounts do not matter.

15
00:00:38,411 --> 00:00:40,361
The ratio between them does.

16
00:00:40,711 --> 00:00:42,743
Tea for one, or tea for ten.

17
00:00:42,743 --> 00:00:45,542
The ratio of milk to
tea leaves stays fixed.

18
00:00:45,942 --> 00:00:49,552
An equilibrium mixture has
its own fixed ratio too.

19
00:00:49,552 --> 00:00:53,216
But in chemistry, the
ratio has a twist: powers.

20
00:00:53,816 --> 00:00:58,080
Let's run three experiments on our molecule
bench, all at the same temperature.

21
00:00:58,430 --> 00:01:03,061
Flask one starts with hydrogen and
iodine, one mole per litre each.

22
00:01:03,461 --> 00:01:05,736
Flask two starts with more hydrogen.

23
00:01:05,736 --> 00:01:08,408
Two moles per litre, with one of iodine.

24
00:01:08,808 --> 00:01:11,631
Flask three starts with
only hydrogen iodide.

25
00:01:12,031 --> 00:01:14,023
Each flask reaches equilibrium.

26
00:01:14,023 --> 00:01:16,376
The final amounts are all different.

27
00:01:16,776 --> 00:01:20,188
Now divide HI squared
by H two times I two.

28
00:01:20,188 --> 00:01:22,151
About fifty, every time.

29
00:01:22,751 --> 00:01:23,664
Why squared?

30
00:01:23,664 --> 00:01:25,406
Try the plain ratio first.

31
00:01:25,756 --> 00:01:31,069
HI divided by H two times I two gives
a different answer in each flask.

32
00:01:31,069 --> 00:01:32,085
No pattern.

33
00:01:32,485 --> 00:01:36,530
Square HI, because the equation
has a two in front of HI.

34
00:01:36,530 --> 00:01:37,937
Now it is constant.

35
00:01:37,937 --> 00:01:40,693
The power comes from
the balanced equation.

36
00:01:41,343 --> 00:01:45,612
In eighteen sixty four, two Norwegian
scientists, Guldberg and Waage, gave

37
00:01:45,612 --> 00:01:46,773
the general rule.

38
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:48,314
The law of mass action.

39
00:01:48,664 --> 00:01:49,564
Step one.

40
00:01:49,548 --> 00:01:51,586
Write the balanced equation.

41
00:01:51,586 --> 00:01:55,058
a A plus b B, double arrow, c C plus d D.

42
00:01:55,808 --> 00:01:56,708
Step two.

43
00:01:56,556 --> 00:01:59,821
Square brackets mean
concentration, in moles per litre.

44
00:02:00,571 --> 00:02:01,471
Step three.

45
00:02:01,283 --> 00:02:03,386
Products go on top, reactants go below.

46
00:02:04,136 --> 00:02:05,036
Step four.

47
00:02:04,998 --> 00:02:08,831
Raise each one to the power
of its number in the equation.

48
00:02:08,831 --> 00:02:11,981
That fraction is K c,
the equilibrium constant.

49
00:02:12,731 --> 00:02:16,075
Now, what happens to K c
when we change the equation?

50
00:02:16,425 --> 00:02:21,895
At seven hundred kelvin, K c for H
two plus I two making two HI is fifty

51
00:02:21,895 --> 00:02:23,330
four point eight.

52
00:02:23,730 --> 00:02:25,219
Reverse the equation.

53
00:02:25,219 --> 00:02:26,878
K c flips upside down.

54
00:02:26,878 --> 00:02:31,484
One over fifty four point eight,
about zero point zero one eight two.

55
00:02:31,884 --> 00:02:33,099
Halve the equation.

56
00:02:33,099 --> 00:02:34,454
Take the square root.

57
00:02:34,454 --> 00:02:36,082
About seven point four oh.

58
00:02:36,482 --> 00:02:37,751
Double the equation.

59
00:02:37,751 --> 00:02:38,651
Square it.

60
00:02:38,522 --> 00:02:39,835
About three thousand.

61
00:02:40,435 --> 00:02:41,335
Compare.

62
00:02:41,145 --> 00:02:44,653
Forward: HI on top, K c
fifty four point eight.

63
00:02:44,653 --> 00:02:48,520
Reverse: HI below, K c zero
point zero one eight two.

64
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:50,109
Pause and think.

65
00:02:50,109 --> 00:02:53,250
A forward reaction has K
c equal to one hundred.

66
00:02:53,250 --> 00:02:55,251
What is K c for the reverse?

67
00:02:58,451 --> 00:02:59,925
Zero point zero one.

68
00:02:59,925 --> 00:03:02,418
Just flip it: one over one hundred.

69
00:03:03,068 --> 00:03:04,114
One more rule.

70
00:03:04,114 --> 00:03:07,401
Change the starting amounts,
and K c stays the same.

71
00:03:07,751 --> 00:03:10,685
Change the temperature,
and K c gets a new value.

72
00:03:10,685 --> 00:03:12,454
So always say the temperature.

73
00:03:13,054 --> 00:03:13,954
Remember this.

74
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:16,287
Products over reactants,
each raised to its power.

75
00:03:16,987 --> 00:03:18,677
Now, one worked example.

76
00:03:18,977 --> 00:03:22,978
At seven hundred kelvin, K
c is fifty four point eight.

77
00:03:22,978 --> 00:03:24,574
Only HI was taken.

78
00:03:24,574 --> 00:03:28,574
At equilibrium, HI is zero
point five moles per litre.

79
00:03:28,574 --> 00:03:30,340
Find H two and I two.

80
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:34,855
Each two HI that break give
one H two and one I two.

81
00:03:34,855 --> 00:03:36,690
So H two equals I two.

82
00:03:36,690 --> 00:03:37,688
Call it x.

83
00:03:38,438 --> 00:03:43,153
Fifty four point eight equals zero
point five squared, over x squared.

84
00:03:43,903 --> 00:03:48,334
x squared is zero point two five
divided by fifty four point eight.

85
00:03:48,334 --> 00:03:51,146
About zero point zero zero four five six.

86
00:03:51,896 --> 00:03:53,003
Take the root.

87
00:03:53,003 --> 00:03:57,619
x is about zero point zero six eight
moles per litre, for both H two and

88
00:03:57,619 --> 00:03:58,519
I two.

89
00:03:58,925 --> 00:04:00,387
Now, the exam trap.

90
00:04:00,737 --> 00:04:02,410
Students forget the power.

91
00:04:02,410 --> 00:04:04,981
They write HI over H two times I two.

92
00:04:05,381 --> 00:04:08,008
The two in front of HI becomes a power.

93
00:04:08,008 --> 00:04:08,958
HI squared.

94
00:04:08,958 --> 00:04:11,364
Always start from the balanced equation.

95
00:04:12,014 --> 00:04:13,479
Where is this asked?

96
00:04:13,479 --> 00:04:17,040
Boards ask you to write K
c and use the reverse rule.

97
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:21,397
Entrance tests ask how K changes
when you flip or scale an equation.

98
00:04:21,997 --> 00:04:23,274
Exam level now.

99
00:04:23,274 --> 00:04:28,339
For nitrogen plus three hydrogen
making two ammonia, K c is sixty four.

100
00:04:28,339 --> 00:04:33,144
Find K c for one ammonia breaking
into half a nitrogen and three halves

101
00:04:33,144 --> 00:04:34,044
hydrogen.

102
00:04:33,966 --> 00:04:35,297
Pause and solve.

103
00:04:40,697 --> 00:04:42,116
The answer is B.

104
00:04:42,116 --> 00:04:44,042
Zero point one two five.

105
00:04:44,542 --> 00:04:46,579
First, reverse the equation.

106
00:04:46,579 --> 00:04:48,903
K c becomes one over sixty four.

107
00:04:49,403 --> 00:04:50,404
Then halve it.

108
00:04:50,404 --> 00:04:51,769
Take the square root.

109
00:04:51,769 --> 00:04:52,814
One over eight.

110
00:04:53,314 --> 00:04:56,014
One over eight is zero point one two five.

111
00:04:56,014 --> 00:04:57,798
C forgot to take the root.

112
00:04:58,398 --> 00:04:59,938
Here is your recap.

113
00:04:59,938 --> 00:05:01,521
Screenshot this card.

114
00:05:04,721 --> 00:05:06,907
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

115
00:05:07,307 --> 00:05:08,207
One.

116
00:05:07,797 --> 00:05:10,670
Who gave the law of mass action, and when?

117
00:05:11,470 --> 00:05:12,370
Two.

118
00:05:11,957 --> 00:05:14,722
Why is HI squared in the K c expression?

119
00:05:15,522 --> 00:05:16,422
Three.

120
00:05:16,034 --> 00:05:18,803
What happens to K c when
you reverse an equation?

121
00:05:19,703 --> 00:05:22,379
Next time: gases are measured by pressure.

122
00:05:22,379 --> 00:05:24,403
Is there a K for pressure too?

123
00:05:24,403 --> 00:05:27,284
We find out in Homogeneous
Equilibria and K p.
